module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.FirstOrderThickeningConormalSelfMap
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.SpecialFibreIdealGenerator

/-!
# A self-arrow of a first-order deformation scales its defining ideal

Let `P` be a deformation of a scheme `X` over an object `A` of `𝒞_Λ` whose maximal ideal is
square-zero and **principal**, generated by `t`. A self-arrow `φ : P ⟶ P` of the deformation
category moves the base: its morphism of total spaces `φ.map` sits in a cartesian square over
`Spec` of its base component `φ.base : A ⟶ A`. Since `φ.base` carries `𝔪_A = (t)` into itself,
`φ.base t = c t` for some `c : A`, and this file concludes that `φ.map^♯` is then
**multiplication by the function `c` determines** on the whole defining ideal of the special
fibre, and hence that the endomorphism of the conormal sections it induces is multiplication by
the image of `c` on `X`.

That is [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3V]'s scaling of the infinitesimal coordinate, read on sections.
The general statement it specialises is
`Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_eq_mul_of_affineOpens_ker_eq_span`, whose three hypotheses a self-arrow
of a deformation category supplies for free:

* `i ≫ φ.map = i` is the `special_compat` field of
  `Deformation.Examples.SchemeDeformationCategory.Hom`;
* `IsClosedImmersion i` is `Deformation.Examples.deformationSpecialMap_isClosedImmersion`, the
  special fibre being a base change of the closed point;
* `i.ker ^ 2 = ⊥` is `Deformation.Examples.ker_specialMap_pow_two_eq_bot` from square-zeroness of
  `𝔪_A`.

The generation hypothesis `hgen` is `Deformation.Examples.ker_app_specialMap_eq_span`, and the
scaling hypothesis `hscal` is the arrow's cartesian square read on global sections, which is
`Deformation.Examples.app_baseSection`.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm`: a morphism lying over a map of affine bases
  carries the function an element of the source base determines to the function its image
  determines. This is a square over affine bases, read on sections.
* `Deformation.Examples.app_baseSection`: that reading at the cartesian square of an arrow of
  deformations.
* `Deformation.Examples.app_specialMap_baseSection`: that reading at the square identifying the
  special fibre, which turns the scalar into a scalar of the residue field.
* `Deformation.Examples.preimage_map_self`: a self-arrow does not move the opens of the total
  space.
* `Deformation.Examples.app_map_eq_mul_baseSection`: **the comorphism of a self-arrow is
  multiplication by the function `c` determines, on the defining ideal of the special fibre over
  an arbitrary open.**
* `Deformation.Examples.conormalSelfMap_eq_smul`: **the induced endomorphism of the conormal
  sections is multiplication by the image of `c` on `X`.**


## Implementation notes

The scalar is carried as an element `c` of the base ring with `φ.base t = c t`, not as an element
of the residue field: that equation is what a computation on the base delivers. The passage to the
residue field happens in the conclusion instead, `Deformation.Examples.app_specialMap_baseSection`
rewriting the scalar as the function the *residue* of `c` determines on `X`; both that and the
scaling hypothesis are readings of one lemma,
`Deformation.Examples.appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm`, at two different cartesian squares.

`c` is **not** assumed to be killed or fixed by anything, and in particular not assumed to lie in
the image of the residue field: only its product with the defining ideal is constrained, which is
all `Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_self_eq_mul_of_ker_eq_span` uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CK2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY7)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Deformation.Examples

variable {Λ k : Type u} [CommRing Λ] [Field k] [Algebra Λ k]
variable {X : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))}

attribute [local instance] deformationSpecialMap_isClosedImmersion

/-! ### A square over affine bases, read on sections -/

/-- **A morphism lying over a map of affine bases carries the function determined by an element of
the source base to the function determined by its image.** Given a commuting square
`m ≫ qW = qZ ≫ Spec g`, the composite `qW^♯` then `m^♯` on global sections is `g` followed by
`qZ^♯`, because `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso_inv_naturality` moves the ring map across the
identification of the global sections of an affine scheme with its ring. Restricting to an open
of the source gives the statement.

This is read twice below: at the cartesian square of an arrow of deformations, where it is the
hypothesis `hscal` of `Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_eq_mul_of_affineOpens_ker_eq_span`, and at the
square identifying the special fibre, where it says that the function a base element determines
restricts on `X` to the function its residue determines. -/
theorem appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] {W Z : Scheme.{u}}
    {qW : W ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of A)} {qZ : Z ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of B)} {g : A →+* B}
    {m : Z ⟶ W} (hm : m ≫ qW = qZ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom g)) (t : A) (V : Z.Opens) :
    (m.appLE ⊤ V le_top).hom (Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap qW t) =
      baseSection qZ (g t) V := by
  have hglobal : (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv ≫ qW.appTop ≫ m.appTop =
      CommRingCat.ofHom g ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv ≫ qZ.appTop := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, hm, Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc]
    exact congrArg (fun z => z ≫ qZ.appTop)
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso_inv_naturality (CommRingCat.ofHom g)).symm
  have hfac : m.appLE ⊤ V le_top =
      m.appTop ≫ Z.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V))).op := rfl
  rw [hfac, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, baseSection_eq_map_baseScalarMap]
  exact congrArg (Z.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V))).op).hom
    (congrArg (fun z : CommRingCat.of A ⟶ Γ(Z, ⊤) => z.hom t) hglobal)

/-- **The comorphism of an arrow of deformations carries the function determined by an element of
the base to the function determined by its image under the base component**, which is
`Deformation.Examples.appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm` at the arrow's cartesian square. -/
theorem app_baseSection {P Q : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X} (φ : P ⟶ Q)
    (t : (P.base : Type u)) (V : Q.scheme.Opens) :
    (φ.map.appLE ⊤ V le_top).hom (Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap P.toBase t) =
      baseSection Q.toBase (φ.base.hom t) V :=
  appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm φ.cartesian.w t V

/-- **The image on `X` of the function determined by an element of the base is the function
determined by its residue**, which is `Deformation.Examples.appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm` at the
square identifying the special fibre of the deformation with `X`. -/
theorem app_specialMap_baseSection (P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X)
    (c : (P.base : Type u)) (V : P.scheme.Opens) :
    (P.specialMap.app V).hom (baseSection P.toBase c V) =
      baseSection X.hom (Deformation.Artin.residueMap P.base c) (P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V) := by
  rw [baseSection_eq_map_baseScalarMap P.toBase c V, Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE,
    ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, Scheme.Hom.map_appLE]
  exact appLE_baseScalarMap_of_comm P.specialCartesian.w c _

/-! ### A self-arrow does not move the opens -/

/-- **A self-arrow of a first-order deformation does not move the opens of the total space.** The
identity and the self-arrow are two lifts of the identity of `X` along the special-fibre
immersion, and two lifts of one morphism have the same preimages
(`Stacks.Thickenings.preimage_eq_of_comm`). -/
theorem preimage_map_self {P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X}
    (hsq : P.specialMap.ker ^ 2 = ⊥) (φ : P ⟶ P) (V : P.scheme.Opens) : φ.map ⁻¹ᵁ V = V := by
  exact Stacks.Thickenings.preimage_eq_of_comm (a' := 𝟙 P.scheme) (a := 𝟙 X.left)
    (j := P.specialMap) hsq
    ((Category.comp_id P.specialMap).trans (Category.id_comp P.specialMap).symm)
    (φ.special_compat.trans (Category.id_comp P.specialMap).symm) V

/-! ### The comorphism is multiplication on the defining ideal -/

/-- **A self-arrow of a first-order deformation whose base component scales a generator of the
maximal ideal multiplies the whole defining ideal by that scalar.** For a deformation `P` whose
base has square-zero maximal ideal generated by `t`, and a self-arrow `φ : P ⟶ P` with
`φ.base t = c t`, the comorphism `φ.map^♯` is multiplication by the function `c` determines on
every section of the defining ideal of the special fibre, over an arbitrary open.

This is `Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_eq_mul_of_affineOpens_ker_eq_span` with its generation
hypothesis supplied by `Deformation.Examples.ker_app_specialMap_eq_span` and its scaling
hypothesis by `Deformation.Examples.app_baseSection`; the specialisation of the two opens is
`B := φ.map ⁻¹ᵁ V`, which turns the `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE` of the general statement
into `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.app`. -/
theorem app_map_eq_mul_baseSection {P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X}
    (hsq : P.specialMap.ker ^ 2 = ⊥) (φ : P ⟶ P) {t c : (P.base : Type u)}
    (ht : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (P.base : Type u) = Ideal.span {t})
    (hb : φ.base.hom t = c * t) (V : P.scheme.Opens) {g : Γ(P.scheme, V)}
    (hg : (P.specialMap.app V).hom g = 0) :
    (φ.map.app V).hom g =
      (P.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le).op).hom
        (baseSection P.toBase c V * g) := by
  have hσ : P.specialMap ≫ φ.map = P.specialMap := φ.special_compat
  have hgen : ∀ (W : P.scheme.affineOpens) (hW : W.1 ≤ φ.map ⁻¹ᵁ V),
      RingHom.ker (P.specialMap.app W.1).hom
        = Ideal.span {(P.scheme.presheaf.map
            (homOfLE (hW.trans (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le)).op).hom
              (baseSection P.toBase t V)} := by
    intro W hW
    rw [baseSection_map P.toBase t (hW.trans (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le)]
    exact ker_app_specialMap_eq_span P ht W
  have h1 : (φ.map.appLE V (φ.map ⁻¹ᵁ V) le_rfl).hom (baseSection P.toBase t V) =
      baseSection P.toBase (φ.base.hom t) (φ.map ⁻¹ᵁ V) := by
    rw [baseSection_eq_map_baseScalarMap P.toBase t V, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
      Scheme.Hom.map_appLE, app_baseSection]
  have hscal : (φ.map.appLE V (φ.map ⁻¹ᵁ V) le_rfl).hom (baseSection P.toBase t V) =
      (P.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le).op).hom
        (baseSection P.toBase c V * baseSection P.toBase t V) := by
    rw [h1, hb, baseSection_mul, baseSection_map P.toBase (c * t) (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le]
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app]
  exact Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_eq_mul_of_affineOpens_ker_eq_span hsq hσ le_rfl
    (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le hgen hscal hg

/-! ### The induced endomorphism of the conormal sections -/

/-- **The endomorphism of the conormal sections induced by such a self-arrow is multiplication by
the image of the scalar on `X`.** The conormal sections of a first-order thickening are its
defining ideal, so `Deformation.Examples.app_map_eq_mul_baseSection` computes the comorphism on
them; `Stacks.Thickenings.eq_conormalSelfMap` turns that computation into one of the induced
endomorphism, the candidate being the scalar multiple of the section one started with. -/
theorem conormalSelfMap_eq_smul {P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X}
    (hsq : P.specialMap.ker ^ 2 = ⊥) (φ : P ⟶ P) {t c : (P.base : Type u)}
    (ht : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (P.base : Type u) = Ideal.span {t})
    (hb : φ.base.hom t = c * t) (V : P.scheme.Opens)
    (s : Γ(Stacks.Thickenings.conormalModules P.specialMap, P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V)) :
    Stacks.Thickenings.conormalSelfMap hsq φ.special_compat V s =
      baseSection X.hom (Deformation.Artin.residueMap P.base c) (P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V) • s := by
  refine (Stacks.Thickenings.eq_conormalSelfMap hsq φ.special_compat V s _ ?_).symm
  rw [← app_specialMap_baseSection P c V,
    ← Stacks.Thickenings.conormalSection_map hsq (preimage_map_self hsq φ V).le,
    Stacks.Thickenings.conormalSection_smul,
    app_map_eq_mul_baseSection hsq φ ht hb V
      (RingHom.mem_ker.mp (Stacks.Thickenings.conormalSection_mem_ker hsq V s))]

end Deformation.Examples

end
